# =============================================================================
#  OSD-TMA.orch - Television Media Analysis (MPAI-OSD V1.5)
#  Workflow Description Language v0.3, AIF V3.0
#
#  One Controller, one Module. The User Agent offers the Controller data identified by
#  Data Type and Port Number, and asks for data identified the same way. It names no AIM.
#
#  The Module is given a television programme as TV Splitting would give it: the pictures
#  (a Basic Visual Object), the sound (a Basic Speech Object whose time is that of the
#  programme) and, if there is one, an auxiliary text that says what the programme is about.
#  The Module analyses the programme as long as it takes and gives the Multimodal Event
#  Descriptors, which grow as the scenes arrive: the last holds them all. The device named
#  "Events" is handed each of them as the Module gives it.
#
#  A step completes before the next begins.
# =============================================================================

workflow OSD-TMA over 1OSD-TMA-V1.5-I01

on Start:

    ask Controller to start

    deliver MultimodalEventDescriptors (OSD-MEV-V1.5:1) to device "Events"

    prompt "Television Media Analysis: give me a programme and I will tell you who speaks when, what is said and what is shown."

    acquire AuxiliaryText (OSD-TXO-V1.5)
    acquire ProgrammeVideo (OSD-BVO-V1.5)
    acquire ProgrammeSpeech (OSD-BSO-V1.5)

    branch on AuxiliaryText {
        offer AuxiliaryText (OSD-TXO-V1.5:1)
    }
    offer ProgrammeVideo (OSD-BVO-V1.5:1)
    offer ProgrammeSpeech (OSD-BSO-V1.5:1)

    loop until Stop:
        wait 2s

on Stop:

    ask Controller to stop
